  "goodToKnow": "Der Baumeister is a master builder or architect, historically the person in charge of building cathedrals or palaces: Karl Friedrich Schinkel was Prussia's great Baumeister, designing much of Berlin's classical centre. Today the usual title is Architekt, though Baumeister remains a professional qualification in Austria. Figuratively, it's the architect of an achievement: Kohl gilt als Baumeister der Einheit. Plural: die Baumeister."
